conch.app carries SwiftTerm 1.11.2 (https://github.com/migueldeicaza/SwiftTerm,
tag v1.11.2, commit b1262db5b6bea699a8260a8c66999436c508ca56), compiled into
the app itself: it is the terminal emulator the Terminal tab of a session conch
hosts draws with. It is conch's only Swift package from outside this
repository, pinned to that exact version in the Xcode project, with its
resolution in project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved.

Why 1.11.2: it is the newest SwiftTerm a stock Xcode builds offline. 1.12.0
onwards ships a Metal shader, which needs Xcode's separately downloaded Metal
Toolchain (`xcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain`), and 1.19.0 onwards
adds a build-tool plugin that xcodebuild refuses to run until it is trusted
(`-skipPackagePluginValidation`). conch doesn't use the Metal renderer.

